messages.content:
Build a HUD-style loader control for Uno Platform, monochrome, in JetBrains Mono:
- a 300-unit reticle: two tick bands that counter-rotate (14 s and 9 s) while the size is unknown, rings, an arc that sweeps every 2.4 s, corner marks and leaders with the percent, the phase and a telemetry line;
- states: Scanning, Locking (the bands stop and an arc fills with the percent), Locked (the X closes in 480 ms, then nothing moves), Idle (dimmed) and Interrupted (keeps its progress and offers Resume);
- a status line with three step dots, announced politely; reduced motion makes Scanning still with a slow pulse;
- the same look as a ProgressRing style at 64, 40 and 24 px;
- a page that simulates a sync (Scan, then Lock to 100%), with Scan / Lock / Idle, Run again and Interrupt, a Light/Dark switch, and a layout for phone and desktop;
- Hot Design previews of every state.

Stack: Uno Platform single project, Material, Toolkit, CommunityToolkit.Mvvm.
